# Worker rules

- Use Redis/BullMQ for execution coordination; persistent job/business state lives in PostgreSQL.
- API creates a persistent job record before enqueuing expensive async work.
- Queue payloads contain IDs and minimal immutable metadata, not giant documents/binaries.
- Workers re-load authoritative state from PostgreSQL.
- Image/video/agent runs must be idempotent/recoverable across worker restarts.
- Use explicit retry policies by failure type. Never blindly retry costly generation after an ambiguous provider response.
- A job must carry/correlate its usage reservation. Completion settles; definite uncharged failure releases; ambiguous provider charge goes to reconciliation/manual-safe state.
- Store generated assets in S3-compatible object storage and metadata in PostgreSQL.
- Concurrency is configured by queue/capability and must respect provider rate limits and cost controls.
